            {"title": "1. You Are the First Teacher", "body_md": "The Church calls parents the *first and best teachers* of their children in the faith. This is not a burden but a grace — and you do not need to be a theologian.\n\nChildren learn faith the way they learn language: by living it with those they love. Your morning prayer, your patience, your kindness to a neighbour — these preach louder than any lesson.\n\nStart where you are. A home where God is spoken of naturally and prayed to daily is already a school of saints."},
            {"title": "2. Prayers to Learn by Heart", "body_md": "Give your child a treasury of prayers to carry for life. Learn them slowly, one at a time:\n\n- **The Sign of the Cross**\n- **The Our Father**\n- **The Hail Mary**\n- **The Glory Be**\n- **The Guardian Angel prayer**\n- **Grace before meals**\n- A simple **Morning Offering** and **Act of Contrition**\n\nRepeat them together until they are as familiar as a lullaby. These prayers become a home the soul can always return to."},
            {"title": "3. The Truths We Believe", "body_md": "Teach the great truths simply:\n\n- **God** is our loving Father who made everything.\n- **The Holy Trinity** — Father, Son and Holy Spirit, one God in three Persons.\n- **Jesus**, the Son of God, became man, died and rose to save us.\n- **The Holy Spirit** lives in us and helps us love.\n- **Mary** is the Mother of Jesus and our Mother.\n- We are made for **heaven**, to be happy with God forever.\n\nThe Apostles' Creed gathers all of this — pray it often together."},
            {"title": "4. The Sacraments and the Commandments", "body_md": "Explain that Jesus gives us **seven sacraments** — special signs that give grace. Children first meet **Baptism**, then **Confession**, **Holy Communion**, and one day **Confirmation**.\n\nTeach the **Ten Commandments** as God's loving rules that keep us safe and happy, summed up by Jesus: *love God* and *love your neighbour as yourself.*\n\nAnd teach mercy in return — the small daily works of love: feed the hungry, comfort the sad, forgive those who hurt us."},
